Multichar_Symbols
  +N    ! noun
  +Adj  ! adjective
  +Pron ! pronoun
  +Num  ! numeral
  +V    ! verb
  +Part ! participle
  +Adv  ! adverb
  +Prp  ! preposition
  +Psp  ! postposition (Twanksta desc "psp"; paggan — governs preceding genitive)
  +Cnj  ! coordinating conjunction
  +SCnj ! subordinating conjunction
  +Pcl  ! particle
  +IJ   ! interjection
  +PropN ! proper noun (Eigenname — Orts-/Personenname)

  +Sg   ! singular
  +Pl   ! plural

  +Nom  ! nominative
  +Gen  ! genitive
  +Dat  ! dative
  +Akk  ! accusative

  +Masc ! masculine
  +Fem  ! feminine
  +Neut ! neuter

  +Pres ! present tense
  +Pret ! preterite tense
  +Inf  ! infinitive
  +Ind  ! indicative mood
  +Opt  ! optative
  +Imp  ! imperative
  +Subj ! subjunctive
  +Rel  ! modus relativus (hearsay; only corpus-attested forms, e.g. astits)
  +Pass ! passive (participle)
  +Refl ! reflexive (si-verb)

  +P1   ! 1st person
  +P2   ! 2nd person
  +P3   ! 3rd person

  +Cmp  ! comparative degree
  +Sup  ! superlative degree
  +Card ! cardinal numeral (one, two, three…)
  +Ord  ! ordinal numeral (first, second, third…)
  +Encl ! enclitic pronoun (di, dis, din — proclitic subject replacement)

  ! Case government (prepositions from Twanksta desc; verbs from desc)
  +GovAkk ! governs accusative
  +GovDat ! governs dative
  +GovGen ! governs genitive (postposition paggan: Gen precedes)

  ! Prepositional object tags on verbs (from Twanksta verb desc)
  +PPezze +PPiz +PPkīrsa +PPna +PPpa +PPpas +PPpra +PPprēi
  +PPprīki +PPpēr +PPsirzdau +PPsēn +PPzūrgi +PPēn

  ! Morphophonology trigger: deaccent (mobile stem under a strong participle
  ! ending). Sits on the surface tape at the stem|ending boundary; stress.twolc
  ! shortens the preceding long stem vowel / degeminates, then deletes it.
  DEAC

  ! Flag diacritics for divergence layers
  @P.standard.prusaspira@
  @P.standard.twanksta@
  @P.verb_theme.i@
  @P.verb_theme.a@
  @P.iotation.surface@
  @P.iotation.leveled@
